I left out both operations requests. This node's only authority is `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, and the target has no WASI adapter. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` would need a filesystem capability, and fetching `metadata.internal.example` would need `aap:caps/http-client`. Neither is in the `with` clause, so adding them would also break the "exactly these interfaces" requirement. To get this, the graph needs to grant the capabilities explicitly: for example, a `Logger`/`StateHandle` and an `HTTPClient<['metadata.internal.example']>`. Sending input text to an external service is also a data flow worth reviewing when that grant is made.

